riving a  real NASCAR race car in Days of Thunder  and according to a profile in Rolling  Stone rode the fastest horse on set  during the climactic land race in Far  and Away it's small potatoes compared to  the stunts he achieves in the mummy and  the mission impossible films and his  other action-based roles but worth  noting so why does he do it during an  appearance on The Graham Norton Show Tom  admitted it all comes down to the  storytelling saying I feel that you're  bringing everything you know physically  and emotionally to a character in a  story I've trained for 30 years doing  stunts and it allows us to put cameras  in places where you are normally not  able to  not only is Tom Cruise a thrilled junkie  but he also loves himself a slick  motorcycle a fact made abundantly clear  when the actor memorably rode a Kawasaki  gpz-900r along an Airport runway in  1986's Top Gun over 35 years later Tom  once again hopped aboard a Kawasaki the  ninja H2 to be exact aka the fastest  motorcycle in the world for the  enormously successful sequel top gun  Maverick in the interim Tom has thrilled  audiences with his astonishing  motorcycle skills in John Woo's Mission  Impossible 2 Joseph Kaczynski sublivion  and Mission Impossible Fallout Tom's  Love for motorcycles extends off screen  as well apparently after wrapping a  project the actor will take home or  purchase the motorcycle used in the film  and add it to his vast collection  according to Notorious Tom has in his  possession the BMW  S1000RR used in Mission Impossible Rogue  Nation the triumph am Thruxton used in  Edge of Tomorrow and yes even that  Kawasaki from Top Gun among others and  if motorcycles don't exist in the  context of the movie Tom will usually  hop on a horse instead but we say that  counts what is a horse if not a  motorcycle with legs  while many of Tom's movies feature the  box office star working alongside a  group of notable co-stars there always  seems to be a moment where his character 